  "notes": "{見破|みやぶ}る means to successfully uncover something hidden — a lie, trick, disguise, or deception.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: [hidden thing]を{見破|みやぶ}る\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {嘘|うそ}を{見破|みやぶ}る: to see through a lie\n- {正体|しょうたい}を{見破|みやぶ}る: to expose someone's true identity\n- トリックを{見破|みやぶ}る: to detect a trick\n- {変装|へんそう}を{見破|みやぶ}る: to see through a disguise\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{見破|みやぶ}っている means 'has already seen through' (resultative state).\n\nGodan verb ({五段|ごだん}): {見破|みやぶ}らない, {見破|みやぶ}ります, {見破|みやぶ}って, {見破|みやぶ}った\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {見抜|みぬ}く: to see through, to perceive (more general; includes positive insights)\n- {暴|あば}く: to expose, to reveal (stronger, often for crimes)",
